.TH XD\-THUMBNAILER 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-thumbnailer \- make a file's thumbnail in a sandbox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-thumbnailer
.OP \-\-size size
.OP \-\-verbose
.I file
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-thumbnailer
makes the freedesktop.org thumbnail of
.I file
(a path or URI) in the thumbnail cache and prints the thumbnail's path.
.BR xd\-files (1)
runs it for the thumbnails the cache doesn't have yet.
.PP
The file is decoded only inside a
.BR bwrap (1)
sandbox with a seccomp filter, without the network and with nothing of the
user's but the file itself: pictures with gdk-pixbuf, other types with the
installed thumbnailers
.RI ( thumbnailers/*.thumbnailer
in the XDG data directories).
Only raw pixels come out of the sandbox; the PNG is written outside it.
When decoding fails, a failure marker is left in the cache, so the file
isn't tried again until it changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " \fIsize\fR"
.B normal
(128 pixels),
.B large
(256, the default),
.B x\-large
(512) or
.B xx\-large
(1024).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Say why a file wasn't thumbnailed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The thumbnail's path was printed.
.TP
.B 1
The file can't be thumbnailed.
.TP
.B 2
The sandbox can't run (for instance, bubblewrap isn't installed), or the
arguments are wrong.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails/
The thumbnail cache (default
.IR ~/.cache/thumbnails ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-files (1),
.BR bwrap (1)
